,"committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-07","committee":"Executive","time":"4.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-20","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-22","committee":"Audit and Governance Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-28","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Cancelled","webcast":true,"url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-07","committee":"Executive","time":"4.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Garden waste fees to increase progressively to \u00a367 by 2027/28, well below neighboring councils' charges","lead":"Progressive fee increases show the council is managing service sustainability through charges. The gap to neighboring councils (\u00a367 vs \u00a375-\u00a394) suggests either deliberate under-pricing or demand resistance, creating income risk if take-up does not meet\u2026","iso":"2026-09-07","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Previously agrred Service Efficiencies &amp; Income Proposals 2026-27","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64115/64115.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Three-weekly waste collection proposal targets \u00a30.265m saving despite uncertain commitment status","lead":"This is a material and potentially contentious service change. If public or political resistance prevents implementation, the \u00a30.265m shortfall would need to be covered elsewhere. Lenders need to know whether this is firm policy or exploratory.","iso":"2026-09-07","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Previously agrred Service Efficiencies &amp; Income Proposals 2026-27","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64115/64115.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Banbury Museum transition creates \u00a30.178m MTFS savings dependent on securing external funding","lead":"Material savings targets depend on an external organization's ability to find alternative funding. This creates contingent liability risk: if the museum cannot secure external support, the council must choose between backfilling or reducing the service.","iso":"2026-09-07","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Previously agrred Service Efficiencies &amp; Income Proposals 2026-27","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64115/64115.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Previously agrred Service Efficiencies &amp; Income Proposals 2026-27","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64115/64115.pdf","headline":"Garden waste fees to increase progressively to \u00a367 by 2027/28, well below neighboring councils' charges","detail":"Building on an already-agreed increase from \u00a349 to \u00a359 in 2026/27, the council proposes further increases to \u00a367 in 2027/28 with potential for gradual future increases. Service levels (25 collections per year) remain unchanged. Neighboring councils charge \u00a370 (Vale of White Horse), \u00a375 (South Oxfordshire), and \u00a394 (Oxford City).","category":"income","matters":"Progressive fee increases show the council is managing service sustainability through charges. The gap to neighboring councils (\u00a367 vs \u00a375-\u00a394) suggests either deliberate under-pricing or demand resistance, creating income risk if take-up does not meet targets.","figures":"Fees: \u00a349 (2026/27), \u00a359, then \u00a367 (2027/28); Neighboring councils \u00a370-\u00a394; Income impact \u00a30.203m (2027/28), \u00a30.228m (2028/29)","quote":"Increase garden waste fees to keep Cherwell's garden waste service sustainable and broadly aligned with neighbouring districts \u2013 providing an increase in income of \u00a30.203m in 2027/28 and \u00a30.228m in 2028/29.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Previously agrred Service Efficiencies &amp; Income Proposals 2026-27","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64115/64115.pdf","headline":"Three-weekly waste collection proposal targets \u00a30.265m saving despite uncertain commitment status","detail":"The council proposes moving to three-weekly collection cycles for residual waste, stated to cut landfill by 14% and boost recycling. The proposal is described as to 'explore' this change, yet appears in the formal MTFS as a 'New Saving' with a specific \u00a30.265m value in 2027/28. This language creates uncertainty about whether the service change is actually committed or still under consideration.","category":"savings","matters":"This is a material and potentially contentious service change. If public or political resistance prevents implementation, the \u00a30.265m shortfall would need to be covered elsewhere. Lenders need to know whether this is firm policy or exploratory.","figures":"\u00a30.265m (2027/28)","quote":"Explore moving to a three-weekly green bin collection to cut landfill by 14%, boost recycling and capture more food waste - providing a saving of \u00a30.265m in 2027/28.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Previously agrred Service Efficiencies &amp; Income Proposals 2026-27","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64115/64115.pdf","headline":"Banbury Museum transition creates \u00a30.178m MTFS savings dependent on securing external funding","detail":"The council is supporting the Banbury Museum to transition to alternative funding sources and reduce council grant dependency from 2027/28 onwards. Savings build from \u00a30.028m in 2027/28 to \u00a30.050m per year from 2028/29 onwards. Success requires the museum to secure external funding; failure would likely require council backfill or service reduction.","category":"other","matters":"Material savings targets depend on an external organization's ability to find alternative funding. This creates contingent liability risk: if the museum cannot secure external support, the council must choose between backfilling or reducing the service.","figures":"\u00a30.028m (2027/28), \u00a30.050m per year (2028/29-2030/31); Total MTFS \u00a30.178m","quote":"Support Banbury Museum to transition to a new operating model of sustainable funding sources by 2027/28, reducing its dependency on council grant funding and building a more resilient, community-driven institution - providing a saving of \u00a30.028m in 2027/28.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Previously agrred Service Efficiencies &amp; Income Proposals 2026-27","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64115/64115.pdf","headline":"Council treasury and investment income strategy contributes \u00a30.5m to 2026/27 budget but does not recur","detail":"The council plans to optimize cash flow and investment strategies to generate higher interest income of \u00a30.5m in 2026/27 only. This material single-year benefit does not appear in future MTFS years. The document does not specify whether this is from higher interest rates, improved cash positioning, or expected investment returns.","category":"income","matters":"Investment income is volatile and sensitive to interest rate and market changes. A one-off \u00a30.5m dependency in a single year represents a specific budget risk if rates fall or cannot be sustained.","figures":"\u00a30.500m (2026/27 only)","quote":"Continue to optimise cash flow and investment strategies through effective treasury management, resulting in higher interest income. This additional revenue will be retained to support the council's general operations - providing a benefit of \u00a30.500m in 2026/27","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-07","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Previously agrred Service Efficiencies &amp; Income Proposals 2026-27","paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64115/64115.pdf","headline":"Pension fund valuation improvement supports \u00a31.0m MTFS savings","detail":"The council has negotiated revised employer pension contributions based on an improved pension fund valuation. This generates \u00a30.500m savings in 2026/27, \u00a30.250m in 2027/28, and \u00a30.250m in 2028/29. The document does not explain the source of the improvement or whether it represents a sustained change in contribution rates.","category":"other","matters":"Pension liabilities are typically one of a council's largest balance-sheet items. An improved valuation and lower contribution rates reduce budget pressure and improve financial position, but lenders need to know if this is one-off or sustainable.","figures":"\u00a30.500m (2026/27), \u00a30.250m (2027/28), \u00a30.250m (2028/29); Total MTFS \u00a31.000m","quote":"Agree revised employer pension contributions based on the improved valuation of the council pension fund -providing a saving of \u00a30.500m in 2026/27, \u00a30.250m in 2027/28 and \u00a30.250m in 2028/29.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-07"},"name":"Cherwell","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-19","since_iso":"2026-08-20","distress":false,"headline":"Garden waste fees to increase progressively to \u00a367 by 2027/28, well below neighboring councils' charges","lead":"Progressive fee increases show the council is managing service sustainability through charges. The gap to neighboring councils (\u00a367 vs \u00a375-\u00a394) suggests either deliberate under-pricing or demand resistance, creating income risk if take-up does not meet\u2026","also":["37 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit and Governance Committee on 2026-09-30","n_findings":38,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 1 - Previously agrred Service Efficiencies &amp; Income Proposals 2026-27","top_paper_url":"https://modgov.cherwell.gov.uk/documents/s64115/64115.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":105,"news_drafts_total":3}}